#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199352} :activity/id #uuid "a8a8cb70-ee8d-5f9c-abbc-e69ac07e7d5f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048940 :topic/id #uuid "cd874833-681f-55d7-862f-73e3a5e38c18" :topic/math-academy-id 4197} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199350 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198420 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198062 :question/id #uuid "8f99f10e-a1bb-5725-a43b-ab556bc3a105" :question/math-academy-id "e-12497"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c8bea365-3b4d-5421-88d0-a4291ba37810" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198658} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198660}] :knowledge-point/title "Metric Units of Time"} :step/id #uuid "3060d590-a664-582a-9f23-370f9b7afe23" :step/math-academy-id 45040 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199380}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199352 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199493 :tutorial/content "**Measuring** means finding a number that describes the size of something. In particular, we determine the duration between two events by measuring the **time** between those events. We use **time units** for this purpose.\n\nThe most popular measurement system within the scientific community is the **metric system**. Within the metric system, the most common units of measurement are called **base units**.\n\nThe base unit for time is the **second**, which we denote using the symbol \"$\\textrm{s}$.\" We measure the time between two events using clocks like the ones shown below.\n\n![](images/93/93026f119d483006ac3e2a58c4b31d68f6a25618afc0b998da74f4914ca1c1c7.png)\n\nWe use **milliseconds** to measure smaller time intervals. The symbol for milliseconds is \"$\\textrm{ms}$.\" The prefix $\\textrm m$ stands for **milli,** which means\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1\\,\\textrm{ms}$ equals\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{1\\,000}\\,\\textrm s\n$$\n\nNotice that if we add $1\\,\\textrm{ms}$ to itself $1\\,000$ times, we get exactly $1\\,\\textrm{s}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1ms + 1ms + ⋯ + 1ms^(⏞)^(1000times) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{1000}s + \\frac{1}{1000}s + ⋯ + \\frac{1}{1000}s &=  \\\\\n1000 \\cdot \\frac{1}{1000}s &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1000 \\cdot 1}{1000}s &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1000}{1000}s &=  \\\\\n&= 1s\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{ms}$ equals $1\\,\\textrm{s}$, as stated in the diagram.\n\nOne millisecond is a very short time interval. To put this into context, a single blink of a human eye is around $200$ milliseconds on average." :tutorial/id #uuid "3f956ba1-1775-5b26-babc-1e86bba4a909" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7790 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "0afe4919-d3e2-5b68-8df5-f2e8fc987517" :step/math-academy-id 45087 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199350}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199360 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198428 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198070 :question/id #uuid "0353f3c2-288d-5107-b292-a685263cf848" :question/math-academy-id "e-12519"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db1c1c29-c709-5d2d-aa49-b018d7d895ae" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198666} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198677}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Conversions Between Time Units"} :step/id #uuid "9191f5f8-499d-51b4-92d1-de7ff06b59cc" :step/math-academy-id 45099} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199380 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199506 :tutorial/content "Other time units in common usage are **minute**, **hour**, **day**, and **week**.\n\nA table showing our units of time is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Second | $\\textrm{s}$ | $-$ |\n| Minute | $\\textrm{min}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{min} = 60\\,\\textrm{s}$ |\n| Hour | $\\textrm{h}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{h} = 60\\,\\textrm{min}$ |\n| Day | $-$ | $1\\,\\textrm{day} = 24\\,\\textrm{h}$ |\n| Week | $-$ | $1\\,\\textrm{week} = 7\\,\\textrm{days}$ |" :tutorial/id #uuid "8ea3f2f4-f2c2-56a5-a55d-05e6deed0927" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7875 :tutorial/title "Other Units of Time"} :step/id #uuid "daea48da-0909-552f-9e43-e00adc50a326" :step/math-academy-id 45413 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186199360}}] :activity/title "Units of Time" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186198502}]}
